            "review_title": "Review at Dong Ho restaurant",
            "review_text": "Rebecca P\nNha Trang, Vietnam69 contributions\n0\nForeigners beware\nJul 2018 • Family\nWe found this restaurant while we were out walking one day and looked at their menu which looked pretty reasonably priced so we decided to celebrate my birthday there with our son and his girlfriend. We ordered three dishes to all share. I have never had oysters so we ordered one for each of us, they were baked and covered with cheese, delicious! I had told my son (who is a chef) before we ordered the dishes to keep up with the cost so there would be no surprises when we got the bill. We are new to Vietnamese Dong so it's a little difficult for us. Before we got our bill he told me it should cost around 600,000 Dong including drinks. Our server then brought our bill and it was 1,087,000 dong. We asked to see the menu and she kept coming up with different excuses. Then we asked for the manager Mr. Ngo Minh Thoai. He came over and still tried to explain why the bill was so high. They said the chefs cooked us extra food because we had four people. They said our fried rice was 310,000 doing because it is a big bowl, which it was not. That's almost $12 for fried rice. My son had enough and said bring me the menu and show me. Then the manager went to the kitchen and all the service staff began to stare at us. We knew what was going on. He came back with a bill of 580,000 dong and apologized. He blamed it on the chef for making meals for four people. I have never heard of a chef walking out into a dinning room and saying,\" oh those plates are for two people, not four, add extra food to their plates and double their bill. The manager did a good job resolving the situation but he should not have blamed it on the chef. He should have been honest and blamed it on the server trying to get us for an extra $20.\nRead more\nService\nFood\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten July 20, 2018",
